{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016NajbuLprNCH37qfhKHrHt","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"4cc27d388fb4a4fe49316791a20127dbb04e31ae","date":"2026-10-02T17:50:09+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-6028: Pass locationsPerRequest to the login location picker and drop numberToShow (#1920)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"560f36f2ca08ed7dd6cd8aa0b43b4a25ec1ed965","date":"2026-09-28T23:03:43+05:30","message":"(fix) Show the location picker from \"Change location\" when chooseLocation is disabled (#1908)","refs":"","body":"With chooseLocation.enabled set to false, the location picker auto-selects the first login location on mount. The header's \"Change location\" link opens the same picker with update=true, so clicking it silently switched the session location to the first location, overwrote the user's saved default, and navigated back without showing a list.\n\nSkip the auto-select effect in the update flow, matching the guard already used by the saved-preference effect.","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"eb16f91793d023f9d8019116cc300e7c14b5d3e8","date":"2026-07-31T00:29:18+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5816: Stop LocationPicker crashing when no login locations are configured (#1818)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Suubi Joshua","authorEmail":"78343336+suubi-joshua@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9dae818f0e30d56c7f31394eda770a3c15c08a8c","date":"2026-06-29T22:05:13+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5767: Redirect to Location header URL on session endpoint calls (#1797)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dilan Kavishka","authorEmail":"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"671bf567c266d51e197359000b73e81d25e080a9","date":"2026-06-08T16:58:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) O3-5645: Prevent open redirect via unvalidated returnToUrl (#1763)","refs":"","body":"* fix(esm-login-app): prevent open redirect via unvalidated returnToUrl\n\nValidate the \\\returnToUrl\\ query parameter before navigating post-login.\nAccept only same-origin URLs whose pathname falls under the configured SPA\nbase path, rejecting external hosts, protocol-relative URLs, and paths\noutside the SPA root.\n\n- Export \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ helper that parses and validates redirect targets\n- Replace unguarded \\\returnToUrl !== '/'\\ check with \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ guard\n- Fall back to \\config.links.loginSuccess\\ when the URL is rejected\n- Add 8 unit tests for \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ covering known attack vectors\n- Add 3 integration tests for open-redirect protection in the component\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): simplify spa base trim in return URL check\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer state in login\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer in location picker\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): encode returnToUrl pathname to prevent query string truncation\n\n* test(esm-login-app): use static encoded string in change-location-link test\n\nUse a hardcoded pre-computed encoded URL string instead of calling\nencodeURIComponent() inside the test assertion. This ensures the test\nactually verifies the production output rather than tautologically\ncomparing the same function call on both sides.\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): prefer node:path over path in vitest.config.ts\n\n* (fix) Allow any same-origin returnToUrl, not just SPA base paths\n\nRemoves the overly restrictive spaBase path check from isSafeReturnUrl.\nSame-origin matching is sufficient to prevent open-redirect attacks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"omeri innocent","authorEmail":"innocentomeri08@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e19d5f0719a035b8dd4abdb0526de38219f937f6","date":"2026-06-05T15:14:05+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5588: Correctly apply Login Location tag filter in useLocationCount (#1734)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar","authorEmail":"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e16e2d9e16a891670bbf4dd0a79ebe81414405d8","date":"2026-05-01T18:32:38+05:30","message":"(test) Add regression tests for 401 Location-header redirect in openmrsFetch (#1754)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ash","authorEmail":"aishwarya.tripathi2023@vitstudent.ac.in"},{"hash":"2fcdf8c24a606f504df5b9d26941e5c256c472ac","date":"2025-11-26T00:56:43+03:00","message":"(fix) Resolve translation infrastructure gaps across multiple packages (#1508)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Resolve translation infrastructure gaps across multiple packages\n\nThis commit fixes several critical translation infrastructure issues that\nprevented proper localization of UI strings.\n\nesm-devtools-app:\n- Wire up translation loading with require.context\n- Add extract-translations script\n- Add translations/en.json with 17 devtools-specific keys\n- Fixes translation fallback-only behavior\n\nesm-help-menu-app:\n- Wire up translation loading with require.context\n- Add extract-translations script\n- Enables help menu translations to load properly\n\nesm-implementer-tools-app:\n- Expand extract-translations glob to include all .tsx/.ts files\n- Add 8 missing translation keys (searchConfiguration, exitUIEditor,\n  objectPropertyValidationMessage, concept/person-attribute search helpers)\n- Wrap hardcoded \"Search configuration\" label with t() function\n\nesm-styleguide (framework):\n- Migrate workspace notifications to use getCoreTranslation()\n- Migrate location picker to use getCoreTranslation()\n- Provides type-safe access to core translations\n- Removes dependency on useTranslation() React hook in framework code\n\nesm-translations (framework):\n- Add errorLoadingLoginLocations to core translations\n\nImpact:\n- Devtools and help menu apps can now be fully translated\n- All UI strings in implementer tools can be extracted for Transifex\n- Framework components use consistent, type-safe translation patterns\n\n* Fixup","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b60b6bd76299ee0662165cb52ff7bb9dd66022f6","date":"2025-11-25T23:03:47+03:00","message":"(feat) Location picker improvements (#1506)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e4d95d7172422e8b6784aff0cb3427c57bbc22cd","date":"2025-08-25T00:47:07+03:00","message":"(fix) Fix change location button text cutoff in navbar","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":44}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4230f134-77dc-4c42-bc58-b9cf303f4180","uuid":"9e0205c5-a457-43f4-b5d8-427d16df84e8","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:51:00.552Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"4cc27d388fb4a4fe49316791a20127dbb04e31ae","date":"2026-10-02T17:50:09+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-6028: Pass locationsPerRequest to the login location picker and drop numberToShow (#1920)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"560f36f2ca08ed7dd6cd8aa0b43b4a25ec1ed965","date":"2026-09-28T23:03:43+05:30","message":"(fix) Show the location picker from \"Change location\" when chooseLocation is disabled (#1908)","refs":"","body":"With chooseLocation.enabled set to false, the location picker auto-selects the first login location on mount. The header's \"Change location\" link opens the same picker with update=true, so clicking it silently switched the session location to the first location, overwrote the user's saved default, and navigated back without showing a list.\n\nSkip the auto-select effect in the update flow, matching the guard already used by the saved-preference effect.","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"eb16f91793d023f9d801